WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.688
So [A.

2
00:00:00.688 --> 00:00:05.640
P.] Tureaud, Jr., when he went down there . . . He said that you couldn’t study.

3
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.240
He said they took turns beating on the walls at night.

4
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.080
And there . . . He had been an A student down in New Orleans.

5
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.860
He said . . . So he just couldn’t study.

6
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:20.200
He said every time his daddy would bring him back [to campus] on Saturdays, it was just like he said, carrying him to the penitentiary.

7
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.160
Bring him back on Sunday and come get him on Friday evening, he said.

8
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.760
Because they just wouldn’t permit him to study.

9
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.120
They just annoyed him.

10
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.260
But now, like with [Lutrill] Payne, Payne said he had no trouble with them.

11
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:36.320
He said sometimes in the dining area, you went in there to eat,

12
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.020
he said there were certain students that would sit there and talk with you.

13
00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:44.420
Because we had some from here that he knew.

14
00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:49.020
Then he said when he went in, if it was just a vacant table, said he just sat there.

15
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.100
He wasn’t looking for company and he just sat there.

16
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.320
So he said he really didn’t have any problem with any of them.

17
00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:03.300
Just like when I went down there, which was year later, fifty-one, two, fifty-three, before I went and graduated in fifty-six.

18
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.180
Well, I had no problem with them.

19
00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.540
Even the girls of the white race, they even studied with us.

20
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.260
So we had no problem whatever.

21
00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:13.760
And you were in graduate school, too.

22
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.065
So there’s a little bit of a more mature . . .

23
00:01:16.065 --> 00:01:17.340
[agrees] Yes, more mature group.

24
00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.300
So you got a letter saying, “You’re accepted . . .”

25
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.000
You saw that didn’t you?

26
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.040
Well, that’s when we sent the picture.

27
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:27.820
In this letter that’s in this book, they said they were sorry but LSU was whites only.

28
00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:28.520
See, they didn’t know.

29
00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:39.340
When he said he was an agriculture teacher in the state of Louisiana and that he wanted to come there because it would kind of enhance his . . . be more at home with what he’s going to expect.

30
00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:46.400
So when they sent that, well, then that’s when the lawyers got busy, you know, saying that we just have to, you know file suit.

31
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.480
And who were your lawyers?

32
00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:47.684
[A.

33
00:01:47.684 --> 00:01:48.500
P.] Tureaud [Sr.]

34
00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.460
And did Thurgood Marshall assist him?

35
00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.420
Thurgood Marshall assisted him.

36
00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.500
So tell me about them.

37
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.760
Tell me about what you remember about them.

38
00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.180
Well, I tell you what they would do.

39
00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:03.300
They would visit our home and they would find out things about how things were going.

40
00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.040
And they were pressing those suits, you know, to do that.

41
00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:14.040
So it was a matter . . . They knew what to do to get these schools open because they knew it was only fair to do that.

42
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.400
So they won every case they had.

43
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.100
They were able to win their cases.

44
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.840
And he just went down there; Payne was just such a person . . . Brave, I guess I wouldn’t have been as brave.

45
00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:27.360
But he just got in his car and drove on down, you know, when it was time for the trial.

46
00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:35.700
So he [the judge] ordered Payne to be admitted to LSU Grad School and he was the first African American admitted to the graduate school.

47
00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:35.980
That’s right.

48
00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.180
And to receive credit in the graduate school.

49
00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.780
He was the first African American to receive credit from the graduate school.
